From: millia ampora <198710911+dappermint@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:10:00 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: enable the
 charge pump buses

The two SC8547D charge pumps sit at 0x6a on i2c12 (i2c@890000, the
secondary pump) and on i2c_hub_0 (i2c@980000, the primary pump). The
queue describes both chips but leaves both buses disabled. Enable the
two buses so that /dev/i2c-N exists for each of them, for a read-only
identification of the chips from user space before any driver exists.
Both charger@6a nodes stay disabled, so no driver binds to address 0x6a
and the kernel itself sends nothing on either bus. What changes at run
time is that each bus's default pin state is applied (gpio66 / gpio67
for i2c_hub_0 and gpio208 / gpio209 for i2c12: i2c function, 2 mA,
pull-up, the settings of stock's active state) and the serial engines
are set up at 400 kHz. The hub wrapper (i2c_master_hub) is already
enabled for i2c_hub_1. The interrupt pins gpio0 and gpio3 are not
touched.
Link: https://github.com/mzakamin-hub/iceland-linux/issues/2
Based-on: DocZ13's identification test, which enables the same two buses
 in a test DTB (iceland-pps-handover, GPL-2.0)

Signed-off-by: millia ampora <198710911+dappermint@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 0aba0b9ca5662d839cdf350ea72d0e06f4b13bae)
(cherry picked from commit dca7303883357c6769106cdaf6435364714cfa04)
(cherry picked from commit 47647aa20fc7f5fde6967de18828fd9f453a0f12)
(cherry picked from commit 9533be286aab5ec42fd173a0020c0d922da246cc)
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts    | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index d115515739de3..64cbed74b440f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -1437,12 +1437,15 @@ &qup_i2c9_data_clk {
 
 /*
  * The secondary SC8547D 2:1 charge pump of the VOOC / SuperVOOC path (stock:
- * sc8547-charger-slave@6A on qupv3_se12_i2c, 400 kHz, IRQ on gpio3). Only
- * described: the bus stays disabled and no driver binds to the chip.
+ * sc8547-charger-slave@6A on qupv3_se12_i2c, 400 kHz, IRQ on gpio3). The
+ * bus is enabled so that /dev/i2c-N exists for read-only tests; the chip
+ * node stays disabled, so no driver binds to it.
  */
 &i2c12 {
 	clock-frequency = <400000>;
 
+	status = "okay";
+
 	sc8547d_secondary: charger@6a {
 		compatible = "southchip,sc8547d";
 		reg = <0x6a>;
@@ -1481,12 +1484,15 @@ backlight@11 {
 
 /*
  * The primary SC8547D 2:1 charge pump, also the VOOC / UFCS PHY (stock:
- * oplus,sc8547d@6A on qupv3_hub_i2c0, 400 kHz, IRQ on gpio0). Only
- * described: the bus stays disabled and no driver binds to the chip.
+ * oplus,sc8547d@6A on qupv3_hub_i2c0, 400 kHz, IRQ on gpio0). The bus is
+ * enabled so that /dev/i2c-N exists for read-only tests; the chip node
+ * stays disabled, so no driver binds to it.
  */
 &i2c_hub_0 {
 	clock-frequency = <400000>;
 
+	status = "okay";
+
 	sc8547d_primary: charger@6a {
 		compatible = "southchip,sc8547d";
 		reg = <0x6a>;
-- 
